• For a matrix Am×n,
rank(A) = No. of l.i. columns = No. of l.i. rows ≤ (min(n, m))
• Rank of a matrix: Largest order of non-vanishing minors of a matrix
• A matrix is of rank k iff there is at least one minor of order k that does not vanish and every minor of order higher than k vanishes.
• A square matrix is of full rank iff its determinant is nonzero.
• A square matrix is nonsingular iff all the rows and columns are linearly independent.
