Full Row/Column Rank and Null Space
• Full row rank: If all rows of the matrix m × n are l.i.
• Full column rank: If all columns of the m × n matrix are l.i.
Null Space of linear operator N (A)
All the elements x ∈ (F n, F ) for which Ax = 0. The dimension of null space is the nullity of A, denoted by ν(A).
• Left and right null spaces: yA = 0 or Ax = 0
• N (A) is a linear space.
• If ν(A) = 0, N (A) has only a zero vector and Ax = 0 has only zero vector as solution.
• If ν(A) = k, N (A) then Ax = 0 has k l.i. vector solutions.
• Null space and range space are the subspaces of (F n, F ) and (F m, F ), respectively.
